mantle rm485
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_brand_fogworth
title bells on purple fingers
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=child
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk counts_chapel_bells_on_berry_stained_fingers
likes blackberries long_walks market_bustle summer_evenings
dislikes flies cold_tea
fears the_last_fly_in_the_cup a_count_stopped_short
hopes a_whole_evening_walk both_paws_full_of_bells
topics pastimes +0.4 season +0.3 family +0.2 dreams +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=frank refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# listens for chapel bells with one hand held open, reserving a berry-dark finger for each stroke.

words
oath! = Squash my berry | Bother that last buzz
saying! = No bell without a finger | A walk goes both ways
berry = one squashy blackberry | a fat purple berry
palm = my open hand | my berry hand
spot = a purple dot | one little stain
cup = the yellow mug | a little tin mug
fly = the blue fly | a shiny fly
cloth = a clean bit of cloth | a cloth lid
basket = a basket rim | the wicker edge
shade = a cool patch | the shade of a barrow
stepstone = a striped step | a smooth step
finger = my shortest finger | my littlest finger
leaf = a folded leaf | a curly leaf
stroke = a deep round note | a slow bell stroke

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : There are enough steps for a walk even if I never go outside town.
opinion @2 festivals for 1 : My ears get music and my tongue gets sugar on the very same day.
opinion @3 houses for 1 : Somebody has to put those tall walls up. I couldn't reach halfway.
opinion @4 merchants against 1 : A whole penny seems a lot for berries that grow for nothing.
opinion @5 times for 1 : A little supper and somebody home to hear my count will do.
opinion @6 strangers mixed 0 : I watch a stranger's ears while I'm counting the bell notes.

grown
line @1 greet.return : Welcome. I'm old enough to keep my count while talking now.
line @2 farewell.return : I'll walk a while after the bells fall quiet.
line @3 answer.how : Finding a decent stretch of evening for myself.
line @4 react.news : Some words are worth hearing twice before I count them.
line @5 decline : I'm afraid I've set that part of my day aside already.

adolescent
line @7 greet.return : My ears can pick your voice out beside a rattling cart.
line @8 farewell.return : I'll take the long steps out behind you.
line @9 react.news : Got the words clear despite the whole market.
line @10 answer.how : Taller than the low barrows. Good for seeing past.

young
line @12 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Hello. I can still hear with my hand up.
line @13 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. No purple on this paw yet.
line @14 greet [here.weather=rain] : You can stand under this fat leaf with me.
line @15 greet.return : Hi. That greeting didn't count as a bell.
line @16 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : It's you. I know even before I turn.
line @17 farewell : Take a berry for the way out.
line @18 farewell.return : Bye. My free paw's waving.
line @19 again.open : You're round my step again.
line @20 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family can see the marks on my hand.
line @21 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here by the basket, down low!
line @22 react.news : I'll hold my finger still while you talk.
line @23 react.news.new : I'd have remembered a noise like that.
line @24 react.news.known : That bit was here before my berry got squashed.
line @25 react.news.doubt : I didn't hear it. I can only say that much.
line @26 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'll leave my nice soft berry here for you.
line @27 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : That makes both my ears stand up.
line @28 answer.how : Purple on one side, happy on the rest.
line @29 decline : I can't do it and still be home in time.
line @30 accept_decline : All right. You keep your own bit.
line @31 sympathise : You can stay on my step till it feels better.
line @32 thank : My nicest berry would be about right for you.
line @33 deflect_thanks : I picked it myself. There's lots.
line @34 preclose : I want to hear if another one's coming.
line @35 accept_preclose : Go on before the evening shrinks.

young

scene purple
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tuck #berry# under my tongue.
b : How long before you eat it?
a : Till the next bell. Sometimes I can't wait that long.

scene finger
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can count five chapel strokes with #palm# open.
b : What happens after five?
a : I get the other hand dirty too.

scene wheels
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : From down here every basket looks like a moving roof.
b : A whole little roofed street for you.
a : Some roofs smell of cheese. I walk close behind those.

scene walk
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want to walk from this step until my legs ask for supper.
b : Will you know how to get back?
a : I'll keep all the doors on one side going out and the other coming home.

scene summer
when topic=season self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Evening stays so long it fits two walks.
b : Where does your second walk go?
a : Round the same houses. I see new shadows.

scene flycup
when topic=food self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #fly# thinks this berry is a stool.
b : Can you cover the berry till you need it?
a : I'll put #leaf# over the top like a little tent.

scene coldcup
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : Cold tea looks like a puddle in #cup#.
b : It might still taste of leaves.
a : It does. Wet ones. I'd like mine warm.

scene mama
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave #spot# by my place so #self.mother# can see which cup is mine.
b : Wouldn't a clean cup do as well?
a : Then I'd have to sit right by it all the time.

scene dad
when topic=family self.father
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've got a counting trick to show #self.father# once the chapel starts ringing.
b : What part needs showing?
a : This little claw goes across my palm to mean one whole hand.

scene moon
when topic=dreams self.owes=yes
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I'm supposed to find money before the moon goes black.
b : Would it help if a grown wolf heard what you owe?
a : Yes. I can show the size of the moon with two fingers but it won't stay that way.

scene stall
when topic=prices
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : How do I tell a whole basket price from a price for one berry?
b : Ask what you'd get for the coin in your hand.
a : That's good. I can show one copper without letting it go.

scene sleep
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I dreamed a bell came into bed and rolled under my back.
b : That must have made a racket when you turned.
a : No sound at all. A waking bell would have made my ears jump.

adolescent

scene scrape
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mark longer walks with little chalk strokes inside the gate.
b : How do you keep another walker from spoiling the count?
a : I mark the height too. The old ones come halfway up my arm.

scene carry
when topic=family
does offer / accept / assess
a : I can carry the berries in a proper bowl these days.
b : I'll let you have the fuller bowl then.
a : Leave me #cloth#. I don't fancy feeding the flies on the way.

grown

scene echo
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a corner where the last chapel note comes back quite clear.
b : Did you ever count that echo twice?
a : I made a business of it once. Now I keep a finger folded for the wall.

scene barrows
when topic=land
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put a lower shelf on a market barrow for children to look along.
b : What would you keep down there?
a : Fallen apples with the bruises in view. Nobody should have to guess what a copper buys.

scene evenfall
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A long light evening still gives me the urge to go out and count something.
b : Bells or berries these days?
a : Doorsteps mostly. I know how far the little legs I remember could manage.

scene days
when topic=prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Market talk is harder to listen to when every price hurts.
b : There's still a street out beyond the costliest stalls.
a : I walk it and look along each wall for brambles. That's one supper I can gather.

young

story stuckfive [topic=pastimes]
  : I once counted six bells and only saw four fingers.
  : Two fingers were stuck with berry juice.
  b : Did the bells have to start over?
  : No. I licked between the fingers and got both counts back.

story leafboat [topic=travel]
  : I put a blackberry on a leaf boat in the gutter.
  : The boat tipped and the water came up purple.
  b : Did the berry go sailing away?
  : Only to my foot. I rescued it with a spoon and gave the boat a lighter passenger.

story quietfly [topic=food]
  : A fly sat on top of my cup cloth and never moved.
  : I lifted the cloth very slowly to scare it.
  b : Did it fly up into your nose?
  : It was a berry seed. I gave it a good scare anyway.

rule @bellpaw
when concept=bark self.job=child
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One up. Two up. Still got fingers.

rule @purplelip
when concept=bark self.likes=blackberries
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Purple tongue. The berry's really gone.

rule @farwalk
when concept=bark self.likes=long_walks
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Another doorstep and then another.

rule @buzzlid
when concept=bark self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Sit on the lid if you must.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : I'm #self.first#. You can see my bell count from here.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I've a finger free for waving.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I can still count the bells if it's too dark to count the spots.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : You stand up there. I hear you fine from my step.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=child] : I walk and listen. A pup's legs get busy enough.
dlg @6 resident.job : Leave me a shred of daylight for walking after my shift ends.
dlg @7 resident.bye : Bye from my clean hand.

graft resident.hub
choice What do the purple marks mean? -> berryhand
node berryhand
say A spot for sitting by the bush. That mark doesn't wash off as soon as a bell count.
choice Which one lasts longest? -> deepmark
choice We can talk about something else. -> hub
node deepmark
say The one under my claw. I can go to sleep and wake with yesterday's berry still saying hello.
choice I'll listen a little longer. -> hub
choice Good evening, then. -> bye
